WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.467
Installing REau, step by step

2
00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:10.333
1. Download the APK from the project’s Releases page and open the file to install it

3
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:22.133
Play Protect may block the installation. In the Play Store, tap your profile picture, Play Protect and the gear. Pause scanning, install the APK and turn Play Protect back on

4
00:00:22.133 --> 00:00:28.067
2. Open REau and scroll the terms of use to the end, or tap Scroll to the end

5
00:00:28.067 --> 00:00:31.067
Then tap I accept

6
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:41.667
3. Allow location while using the app: it is only used to find the dash’s Wi-Fi. If Android asks, also allow the suggested Wi-Fi networks

7
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.200
4. Tap Turn on and allow notifications

8
00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:51.867
5. The Android Auto server is turned on by hand: tap Open Android Auto settings

9
00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:57.600
The first time, scroll to the bottom and tap Version ten times. Confirm with OK

10
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:03.800
In the three-dot menu, tap Start head unit server. If it is already on, the item becomes Stop

11
00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:10.133
Developer mode is only the first time. After that, each time, the three-dot menu is enough

12
00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:19.133
6. Go back to REau. The first time, Android asks Connect to device: tap Connect so REau can join the dash’s Wi-Fi

13
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:23.267
With Android Auto Active and the dash Ready, REau is Streaming

14
00:01:23.267 --> 00:01:28.400
7. In Permissions, tap Ask for the missing ones and allow everything

15
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:34.667
Also leave REau out of battery optimization, so Android doesn’t pause the app with the screen off

16
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:42.667
8. On the Android Auto screen, the Fit assistant checks that the maneuver arrow and the speed show whole on the dash

17
00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:48.000
All set. Set the route in Waze and put the phone away. To stop, tap Turn off

